          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at 10 years of age. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately once per month. The etiology is unknown. The epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:  \n- Carbamazepine  \n- Brivaracetam  \n\nSeizure Burden Summary:  \nApproximately one focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizure per month.\n\nAssessment:  \nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy of unknown etiology, with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 10.\n\nPlan:  \nContinue carbamazepine and brivaracetam. Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
